Purpose: Read retained paginated rollout usage once and serve shared calendar, model-cost, approximate weekly-quota and actual credit-deduction reports to app-server clients.

Requires: Unit:cross/materialize-model-catalog-from-local-file

Provides: Count authoritative native completed and incomplete response records without waiting for deferred snapshots or billing delivery twice, apply ccusage-style changed-cumulative reported-last accounting and cumulative-only fallback to historical snapshots, and retain observed official spending-only increments when installed last usage stays unchanged. Read active and nested archived plain JSONL without duplicate discovery at observed lengths without decoding unrelated conversation bodies, use response thread ownership instead of subagent projection ordinals for copied records, preserve referenced-history suffixes and legacy parent replay exclusion, and retain unknown models and malformed-record diagnostics. Resolve preceding thread-owned applied model settings at native task starts while preserving an in-flight response context model and never relabeling earlier spending from later settings. Price exclusive cache buckets by inclusive model tiers, anchor paired quota and credit observations to response arrival rather than deferred snapshot delivery, aggregate calendar periods at response arrival with preceding-request boundaries, identify weekly cycles by reset time within a five-minute tolerance, estimate all retained Pro-family quota cycles from multiple local spans without amplifying missing-record gaps through global overlapping pairs, exclude ambiguous stale-cycle intervals without freezing later current-cycle measurements, close weekly cycles at credit decrease with exhausted quota, exclude credit-funded quota intervals without losing totals, retain continuous credit periods without delayed-balance duplication, cache exact per-model details from the once-priced retained timeline, derive whole-cycle Unrecorded spending from Estimated times Used divided by 100 minus Observed with a zero floor, and serve process-wide usage/read snapshots with explicit refresh, fresh-versus-cached evidence, latest usage time, complete build duration and scan errors. Report real build phases and completed candidate-file counts through bounded, latest-only usage/buildProgress notifications correlated to the incoming usage/read request and sent only to its connection.

Boundary: Native rollout persistence and response identities remain the input owner; projection-only subagent ordinals do not prove billing ownership. Reports consume response records and unmatched token_count snapshots, retain the pricing document and native referenced-history semantics, make no network request, and invent neither missing usage nor prices or deductions across missing or conflicting balances. Native background-compaction budget charges without rollout usage remain outside reports. Used, Observed and Estimated are independent observations rather than an arithmetic identity. Quota observations and spending require Pro, ProLite or ProMax with a primary weekly window; other plans and unknown plans still retain ordinary usage and credit accounting. Period details retain unknown models, exclude the ending request and credit-funded quota gaps, and need no additional scan or pricing pass. Only a successful complete build replaces the shared snapshot and measured duration. Older server snapshots may lack duration and model details. TUI views, response recording and successful-output publication remain independent. Progress performs no second file scan or per-record notification, does not cancel an admitted shared build when its UI is hidden, and never substitutes request wait time for producer build duration.

Verification: Reader and wire tests cover historical subagent projection headers, referenced suffixes, native response thread ownership, ccusage last-first and cumulative-only selection, context-only legacy snapshots, zero-context and resumed incomplete spending with and without response IDs, explicit model retention, preceding applied model settings, task-boundary model selection, foreign and absent model ownership, deferred snapshots, standalone compaction, repeated delivery, malformed input and large unrelated payloads. Aggregate, quota and credit tests retain per-response pricing, copied-record deduplication, calendar attribution, credit completion and exclusion, delayed recovery, continuous credit periods, preceding-request boundaries, mixed and unknown models, long-context partitions and older snapshot fields. Quota tests cover Pro-family admission, all retained cycles, whole-cycle Unrecorded spending and its zero floor, and compare complete and locally missing datasets across thousands of records, rounding phases and uneven sampling; measured complete-report build durations preserve the existing speed requirement. Service tests retain shared explicit-refresh snapshots, measured build duration including zero, serialization and scan-error recovery. Progress checks cover real stage transitions, candidate-file totals including skipped files, complete publication and error behavior, cached reads, request correlation, connection isolation and bounded notification cadence; paired measurements assess observer overhead without changing accounting results.

